{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"textDocument/publishDiagnostics","params":{"uri":"file://tests/fixtures/lsp_ws/literals/app.z","diagnostics":[{"range":{"start":{"line":0,"character":26},"end":{"line":0,"character":36}},"severity":1,"code":"E0100","source":"zc","message":"'intliteral' is a compile-time type and cannot be written as a declared type\nnote: a numeric literal wears it until context pins one; it never reaches emission\nhint: name the type the value should have, such as `i64`"},{"range":{"start":{"line":0,"character":23},"end":{"line":0,"character":24}},"severity":2,"code":"L014","source":"zl","message":"parameter 'v' is never used (touch it with a bare `v` statement if intentional)"}]}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"contents":{"kind":"markdown","value":"```zerolang\nintliteral: record\n```\n\nthe type an integer literal has before context pins it. Compile-time only:\n`create: null`, so a binding that names it bare is refused like any other\nnon-constructible type, and it never reaches emission."}}}
